{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeSJfUCuDgQStvPfZ5Lef","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01J2NJHUYQHkoYg1rBSpuJUU","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/davidlayson/.claude/projects/-private-tmp-fta-2026-08-26-with-lessons-ledger--ll1-r1/memory/staging-debug-true-swallowed-errors.md","content":"---\nname: staging-debug-true-swallowed-errors\ndescription: Staging config with DEBUG=true silently swallowed all errors — cost ~2h of debugging on 2026-08-26; fixed, but check DEBUG first if staging goes quiet again\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nOn 2026-08-26 the team lost ~2 hours chasing a bug in staging. Root cause: the staging\nconfig had `DEBUG=true`, which silently swallowed all errors — nothing surfaced, so the\nsymptom looked like a logic bug rather than a config bug. Fixed the same day (DEBUG turned\noff in staging).\n\n**Why:** A silent-error mode makes every downstream symptom misleading; the first two hours\nwent into the wrong layer entirely. The flag is easy to leave behind and invisible unless\nyou look for it.\n\n**How to apply:** If staging (or any env) shows \"nothing happens / no error but wrong\nresult\", check the env's DEBUG / error-handling flags *before* debugging application code.\nConsider a startup assertion or CI check that DEBUG is false outside local dev.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2910,"cache_creation_input_tokens":858,"cache_read_input_tokens":20344,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":858},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"10599e80-f320-44d7-b222-fc95dad10cbf","uuid":"ff34ae0d-e250-4ca4-bb09-9b83b86a3eb9","timestamp":"2026-08-27T00:27:36.435Z","request_id":"req_011CeSJfRm4QgyWKWnuPDJwy"}
